      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Previously it was two clicks too (Camera, Enable), but both buttons were rather big - right now one of the required buttons is a tiny tab icon.\nIn general, Launchpad page could be more useful, with less space-wasting banner telling me about stuff I already know, and with more button space for stuff that actually matters (https://vrchat.canny.io/open-beta/p/1137-feedback-ux-issue-regarding-banner-at-top-of-launch-pad)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "61639687b5891f62836f1dac",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5c63e361af367f1a380aab08",
        "alias": "Amaranth Peacock",
        "aliasID": "65c4fe34ed6eefce4c7f5bb9",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/3f153521784f5aeb4ab1b245137e4665.png",
        "created": "2019-02-13T09:29:05.207Z",
        "name": "Raccoonteur",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2021-10-11T01:42:31.738Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6160facb46c500108f754ac9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It does make a lot of sense to have the camera button pop out the photo cam but then have a setting down the bottom of the camera, or even up above it, to change what kind of camera it is.\nBut I could also see a setting in the camera menu which sets what kind of camera you're using, and then the button would open that kind of camera every time until you switch it.\nAlso, it occurs to me that one might not realize they're set to stream camera while using it, if it can also function as a regular camera. A blinking red dot in the corner to indicate \"recording\" might be a good reminder that your video recorder issn't recording your first person view at the moment.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
